TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Reproduced the cp-smoke failure in-container and isolated it to a probe defect in scripts/run-smoke.sh rather than in the engine under test. Evidence: I re-ran the checkpoint's in-container python against a scratch /results mount (image localhost/flashnext:dev, the same image cp-build receipted). podman exited 0; four of five probes passed (arch gfx1151/on_cdna=false, fp8_cast e4m3fn_alloc_and_cast=true, registry model_arch_registered=true, aperture ttm_pages_limit=33554432). The fifth failed with `TypeError: cannot unpack non-iterable bool object` at the `ok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym)` line of the admission() probe. The engine itself admitted correctly on the very same run — stdout carries `INFO [triton_moe.py:177] TritonExperts: admitting block-FP8 fused MoE (...) on gfx1151 via in-kernel bf16 upcast`. The contract mismatch is in the probe: patches/0008 defines `_supports_quant_scheme` as a plain boolean predicate (its own pinned tests assert `assert TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(*BLOCK_FP8_SCHEME)` and `assert not ...` directly), so the two-tuple unpack in the smoke script can never succeed. Consequence chain matches the capture exactly: try_() catches the TypeError, sets status=fail, the receipt lands at results/receipts/failed/smoke.json instead of results/receipts/smoke.json, the trailing verifier finds no passing receipt and exits 1 — which is why the archived capture shows only `smoke receipt: .../results/receipts/smoke.json (fail receipts land under results/receipts/failed/)` with an empty stderr and exit 1. Blocked rather than retry for two independent reasons: cp-smoke is kind=checkpoint with a worklist-fixed argv and a brief that forbids repository modification, so it holds no authority to edit the script; and scripts/run-smoke.sh appears in no task's conflictDomains in silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json (host-tooling owns only scripts/run-tp2.sh, proxy-tooling owns scripts/make-proxy.sh and scripts/run-proxy.sh, usb4stream-bench owns scripts/receipts-verify.py), so no existing lane can land the fix either. A retry of cp-smoke would reproduce the identical TypeError, since HEAD equals baseRev 1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304 and the diff is empty. The fix is a one-line contract correction in the probe plus a deterministic-timestamp change to satisfy checkpoint purity; it needs an amendment task holding scripts/run-smoke.sh.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/run-smoke.sh"],"goal":"Grant a short implementation lane authority over scripts/run-smoke.sh and correct the admission probe so the in-container smoke grades the engine instead of tripping over its own call contract. Required changes: (1) In the admission() probe, stop unpacking the return of TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme as a two-tuple. The fork's hook (patches/0008) is a plain boolean predicate, as its own pinned tests assert. Call it as `admitted = bool(TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym))` when the attribute exists, and keep the existing missing-hook fallback reporting fp8_block_moe_admitted=false with reason 'no hook'. Preserve the receipt's data.admission shape ({\"fp8_block_moe_admitted\": bool, \"reason\": str}) so downstream receipt graders keep working; supply a reason string derived locally (for example 'bool predicate admitted' / 'bool predicate refused') rather than a value returned by the hook. Do not weaken the probe into a pass-by-default: a false predicate must still set status=fail and route the receipt to results/receipts/failed/. (2) Satisfy OVERSEER STANDING NOTE 2 (checkpoint purity) for results/receipts/smoke.json: the receipt's ts must not be a fresh strftime on every run. Before writing, read any existing committed results/receipts/smoke.json; if every measured fact in data is byte-identical to the new measurement, reuse the existing ts and rewrite the file byte-identically (or skip the write) so a re-run over an already-correct base leaves tracked files unchanged and exits 0. Only stamp a new timestamp when a measured fact actually changed. (3) Land the resulting passing receipt at results/receipts/smoke.json in the lane commit, and leave the trailing verifier's failed/-beats-passing precedence logic intact. Do not touch patches/, container/, or any engine source: the engine behaviour is already correct and was observed admitting block-FP8 fused MoE on gfx1151 during reproduction.","acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"smoke-admission-contract","description":"The smoke script no longer unpacks the boolean _supports_quant_scheme hook into a two-tuple, still calls the hook, and remains syntax-clean.","argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n scripts/run-smoke.sh && grep -q '_supports_quant_scheme' scripts/run-smoke.sh && ! grep -Eq '(ok|admitted)[[:space:]]*,[[:space:]]*why[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*TritonExperts\\._supports_quant_scheme' scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},{"id":"smoke-runs-green","description":"The in-container smoke runs to completion and exits 0 against the cp-build image.","argv":["bash","scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},{"id":"smoke-receipt-pass","description":"A passing receipt exists at results/receipts/smoke.json, records fp8_block_moe_admitted true, and no fail receipt shadows it.","argv":["bash","-euc","python3 -c \"import json,os,sys; r=json.load(open('results/receipts/smoke.json')); assert r['status']=='pass', r['status']; assert r['data']['admission']['fp8_block_moe_admitted'] is True, r['data']['admission']; assert not os.path.exists('results/receipts/failed/smoke.json'), 'fail receipt shadows the pass'\""]},{"id":"smoke-idempotent-on-tracked-paths","description":"Re-running the smoke over an already-correct base leaves every tracked file byte-identical, per checkpoint purity.","argv":["bash","-euc","bash scripts/run-smoke.sh >/dev/null && git diff --quiet -- . && git diff --quiet --cached -- . && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no)\""]}],"dependencies":["cp-build"]}}
